## Repository Structure

```
{{PROJECT_NAME}}/
├── config-global.json           # datasets, checkpoints, methods, smoke
├── src/{{MODULE_NAME}}/         # all main code
├── third_party/                 # methods from config-global.json
├── configs/                     # experiment yaml
├── scripts/                     # dm_pack.py, dm_push.sh, dm_status.sh, ...
├── slurm/                       # sbatch job scripts
├── tests/
├── data/          ┐
├── checkpoints/   ├─ gitignored, machine-dependent, built by dm_link.py
├── outputs/       ┘ one directory per run: outputs/<run-name>/
├── .docs/
│   ├── progress.md              # timetable + log + todos — committed
│   ├── figures/
│   ├── latex-draft/
│   └── runs/<run-name>/         # promoted keepers — committed
├── instructions.md              # agent coding standards
├── pyproject.toml
├── .python-version
├── README.md
├── .gitignore
└── HANDOFF.md                   # this file
```

Layout owned by `general-codebase-structure`; `data/`, `checkpoints/` and
`outputs/` are materialised per machine by `data-management`.

### .docs/

`.docs/progress.md` is the single source of truth: a gantt timetable at the
top, a dated log in the middle, todos at the bottom — all three sharing the
same section names. Everything else in `.docs/` supports it.

`.docs/` is dot-prefixed and hidden by default in Obsidian and most file
browsers; enable "Show hidden files" to see it.

